= Water Quality Compliance

Drinking water quality is monitored at treatment works, service reservoirs and customer taps according to the sampling plan agreed with the drinking water regulator. This chapter summarises the results for 2025 and describes the events that required investigation.

== Sampling programme

A total of 31,840 samples were taken and analysed for microbiological and chemical parameters. Sampling at customer taps follows a random daytime method, and the addresses are drawn each month by the laboratory information system. Samples at treatment works and service reservoirs are taken at fixed points that are checked for representativeness every year.

Results for Ravensgill have been restated for November after a meter calibration error was found. Spare parts for the equipment at Ravensgill are now held at the Upland depot to shorten repair times. A study of options for Yarrowby is planned, with a report due to the operating board in October. Seasonal variation at Yarrowby was more pronounced than usual because of the dry spell in late June. Detail for Pellow Down and the other sites in the Central zone is held in the operational database.

