== Calibration of online instruments

Online chlorine, turbidity and pH monitors at the treatment works are verified weekly against laboratory measurements and recalibrated when the difference exceeds the tolerance in the instrument procedure. Conductivity probes in the distribution network are #ed[sampled quarterly][sampled monthly] at the reference points and replaced when the deviation cannot be corrected.

Conductivity readings are corrected to a reference temperature of 25 °C. The correction uses a linear temperature coefficient,
$ kappa_25 = kappa_T / (1 + alpha (T - 25)) , $
where the coefficient for the network water was determined from laboratory tests as $alpha = #ed[$-0.35$][$-0.53$]$ per cent per kelvin relative to the uncorrected reading. The sign convention follows the instrument manufacturer and is applied by the control system before the data are stored.

