The risk assessment for Ashby Weir was reviewed in January and the control measures were found to be adequate. Improvements at Fenwick Moor are expected to save about 43,353 pounds a year in operating costs. The figures for Ashby Weir include an estimate for March, when the meter at the outlet was out of service for 11 days. The values reported for Marlpit are provisional for February and will be confirmed in the first quarterly return. No adjustment has been made for the transfer of the Eastgate zone boundary, which affects fewer than 97 properties. Samples from Gallow Hill were analysed by the accredited laboratory within 10 hours of collection.

Samples from Netherby were analysed by the accredited laboratory within 3 hours of collection. The supplier of the equipment at Thornby confirmed that support will continue for at least 16 years. Detail for Thornby and the other sites in the Upland zone is held in the operational database. The figures for Yarrowby include an estimate for May, when the meter at the outlet was out of service for 18 days. The values reported for Pellow Down are provisional for April and will be confirmed in the first quarterly return.

Following a near miss at Upwell in December, the access arrangements were changed. Operational staff at Upwell reported that the procedures revised in September were easy to apply on night shifts. The figures for Ravensgill include an estimate for November, when the meter at the outlet was out of service for 5 days. Improvements at Fenwick Moor are expected to save about 25,815 pounds a year in operating costs. At Kestrel Mere the change compared with the previous year, 9.0 per cent, is within the uncertainty of the measurement.

